   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUSTAIN Tanzania is a multidisciplinary organization that operates in all social, economic, cultural, and environmental realms. These functions attract interest from all spheres, thereby contributing to SUSTAIN&apos;s distinctiveness as an emerging and prospective organization in Tanzania. SUSTAIN&apos;s (SUSTAIN&apos;s) emphasis on participatory and people-centered approaches and cooperation with its beneficiaries is another distinguishing feature that is essential to achieving its vision and mission. In line with this, SUSTAIN believes in and prioritizes collaborative partnerships with groups, networks, and other formal organizations in order to achieve the desired outcome. Through this method, any desired changes and work-related milestones can be attained quickly and effectively. Moreover, SUSTAIN Tanzania is distinguished by its innovative and research-driven approach to addressing community challenges. SUSTAIN aspires to operate based on evidence and create diverse untapped opportunities (such as by utilizing available ICT tools) that promote personal growth. The Governance Manual of the Board of Directors guides the SUSTAIN governance structure. This manual describes SUSTAIN&apos;sorganizational structure and the implementation of technical and financial decisions. There are three major decision-making organs within SUSTAIN. The Annual General Meeting of Members is the supreme body of SUSTAIN, charged with approving matters initiated by the Board of Directors. The Board of Directors consists of five members with strategic, fiduciary, and oversight responsibilities. TheBoard of Directors is generally responsible for the management and control of SUSTAINTanzania&apos;s affairs. It approves and directs the management, which is led by the Executive Secretary/Director. The primary responsibility of the Management Team is to implement policies, rules, regulations, programs, and decisions as approved by the Board and Annual General Meeting (AGM) in order to achieve the goals and mission of SUSTAIN Tanzania.</narrative>
